Equation 30.5a shows the connection between the fitness landscape (the mean fitness surface) and $  eta $ when z is MVN. A similar connection with $  eta $ occurs (when z is also MVN) with the individual fitness surface. Here $  eta $ as the average gradient of individual relative fitnesses (over the population distribution of phenotypes), $$  eta=E_{\mathbf{Z}} igg[
abla_{\mathbf{Z}}[w(\mathbf{z})] igg]=\int
abla_{\mathbf{Z}}[w(\mathbf{z})]\varphi(\mathbf{z})\mathrm{d}\mathbf{z} $$ which holds provided $ z \sim MVN $ (Lande and Arnold 1983). To see this, we use integration by parts to yield $$ \int_{\mathbf{a}}^{\mathbf{b}}
abla_{\mathbf{z}}[w(\mathbf{z})]\varphi(\mathbf{z})\mathrm{d}\mathbf{z}=w(\mathbf{z})\varphi(\mathbf{z}) igg|_{\mathbf{a}}^{\mathbf{b}}-\int_{\mathbf{a}}^{\mathbf{b}}
abla_{\mathbf{z}}[\varphi(\mathbf{z})]w(\mathbf{z})\mathrm{d}\mathbf{z} $$
